Round 163c: the stl_pair.h:543 drop is fixed (__is_constructible for
classes, same-signature constructor templates); the remaining
stl_vector.h:1852 `_Storage' drop (vector::_Temporary_value's union
constructor) is fixed by the union-constructor change
(cpp11_union_constructor_leaves_other_variant_member_uninitialized).
N5008 [pairs.pair]/5 + [temp.inst]/3-4: pair's default constructor is a
constrained template (`template<class U1 = T1, class U2 = T2,
enable_if_t<is_default_constructible<U1> && ...>> pair()'); for
pair<symbolish, unsigned long> the constraint is false and the constructor
is neither viable nor used, so its definition is never instantiated.  The
front end instantiates it anyway when std::vector<pair<...>> is
instantiated, fails on `first()' ("found no match for symbol
'symbolish'") and reports a dropped body (stl_pair.h:543, 8 cbmc-cpp descs
in the round-163 audit).  The verdict is right; the spurious drop hides
real drops in these tests.  This is the libstdc++ shape of main.cpp
(see test.desc): vector's nested _Temporary_value::_Storage has a member of
the element type.
Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51).
